[Event "01. The Lucena: build a bridge (1/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3K1k2/3P2R1/8/2r5/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "01. The Lucena: build a bridge (1/4)"]
[LineDescription "Rook to the 4th rank: the bridge shelters your king from the checks, and the pawn queens."]

{[%csl Gg4] Welcome! Rook and pawn against rook: three ideas every player needs.
You play White in every line. First the Lucena. Your pawn is one step from
queening, your king stands in front of it. The king must step out, and then the
black rook checks it from behind. So first put your rook on the 4th rank: later
it can block the checks. That is the bridge. Blue: the file that keeps the black
king away. Green: where your rook goes.} 1. Rg4 {Rg4 — Build the bridge: your
rook goes to the 4th rank.} 1... Rc3 {[%csl Gf4]} 2. Rf4+ {Rf4+ — Check: the
black king steps away and is cut off.} 2... Kg7 {[%csl
Bf1,Bf2,Bf3,Bf5,Bf6,Bf7,Bf8]} 3. Ke7 {Ke7 — Your king steps out, still next to
the pawn.} 3... Re3+ 4. Kd6 Rd3+ 5. Kc6 {Kc6! — Not Ke5: Black takes the pawn.}
5... Kg8 {[%csl Gc4]} 6. Rc4 {Rc4! — Shield your king: the rook blocks checks on
the c-file.} 6... Kh8 7. Kc7 {Kc7! — Not d8=Q+: Black takes the queen.} 7... Kh7
8. d8=Q {[%also d8=R] d8=Q — Queen! The win is safe.} *

[Event "01. The Lucena: build a bridge (2/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
