[Event "03. The skewer (1/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "R7/P4k2/8/1K6/8/r7/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. The skewer (1/4)"]
[LineDescription "Clear the queening square: if the black rook takes the pawn, a check on the 7th rank wins it."]

{[%csl Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bg7,Bh7] Your rook stands in front of your pawn, the
black rook behind it. While your rook blocks the pawn, it cannot queen. Move the
rook off the queening square, but choose the square well: if the black rook then
takes the pawn, your rook should check along the 7th rank, and the black rook
behind the king falls. Blue: the 7th rank, where the trap is sprung. Green: the
square of the winning check.} 1. Rh8 {Rh8! — If ...Rxa7, Rh7+ wins the rook.}
1... Rxa7 2. Rh7+ {Rh7+! — Check: the rook behind the king falls.} 2... Ke8 3.
Rxa7 {Rxa7 — The rook is won: the win is safe.} *

[Event "03. The skewer (2/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "7R/4k2P/2K5/7r/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "03. The skewer (2/4)"]
[LineDescription "Clear the queening square: if the black rook takes the pawn, a check on the 7th rank wins it."]

{[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Bf7,Bg7] Black checks before it takes the pawn: walk your
king out of the checks.} 1. Rc8 {Rc8! — Not Rg8: Black takes the pawn.} 1...
Rh6+ 2. Kb7 {Kb7! — If ...Rxh7, Rc7+ wins the rook.} 2... Rxh7 3. Rc7+ {Rc7+! —
Check: the rook behind the king falls.} 3... Kf8 4. Rxh7 {Rxh7 — The rook is
won: the win is safe.} *

