{[%csl Ba7,Bb7,Bd7,Be7,Bf7,Bg7] One more: set the trap, escape the checks, win
the rook.} 1. Ra8 {Ra8! — If ...Rxh7, Ra7+ wins the rook.} 1... Rh6+ 2. Kf5
{Kf5! — Not Ke7: Black takes the pawn.} 2... Rxh7 3. Ra7+ {Ra7+! — Check: the
rook behind the king falls.} 3... Kd8 4. Rxh7 {Rxh7 — The rook is won: the win
is safe.} *

[Event "04. The Philidor: check from behind (1/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/1k2r3/R1p5/8/2K5 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. The Philidor: check from behind (1/4)"]
[LineDescription "Once the pawn reaches your 3rd rank, check from far behind: the black king cannot hide."]

{[%csl Ga8,Ga7,Ga6] Now you defend: Black has the pawn, you hold the draw. While
the pawn is on your 4th rank, your rook on the 3rd rank keeps the black king
out. Once the pawn steps to the 3rd rank, the king can no longer hide in front
of it: send your rook far up the board and check from behind. If the king walks
towards your rook, it leaves its pawn. Green: every square from where your rook
holds the draw.} 1. Ra8 {[%also Ra7,Ra6] Ra8! — Go far behind the king: check
from a distance. Ra6 and Ra7 also hold.} 1... Kb3 2. Rb8+ Rb4 3. Rxb4+ {[%also
Ra8,Rc8,Rd8,Re8,Rf8,Rg8,Rh8]} 3... Kxb4 4. Kc2 Kc4 5. Kc1 {Kc1! — Not Kd1: you
end up in zugzwang.} 5... Kb3 6. Kb1 {Kb1! — Black is in zugzwang: it must move,
so it cannot win.} 6... c2+ 7. Kc1 Ka2 8. Kxc2 {Kxc2 — The pawn falls: a draw.}
*

[Event "04. The Philidor: check from behind (2/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3r4/8/8/8/5k2/4Rp2/8/5K2 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. The Philidor: check from behind (2/4)"]
[LineDescription "Once the pawn reaches your 3rd rank, check from far behind: the black king cannot hide."]

{[%csl Ge7,Ge6] Keep checking from behind until the pawn falls.} 1. Re7 {[%also
Re6] Re7! — Go far behind the king: check from a distance. Re6 also holds.} 1...
Kg3 2. Rg7+ Kh4 3. Rh7+ {[%also Rf7,Re7,Rc7,Rb7,Ra7,Rg6,Kg1,Kf2,Ke1]} 3... Kg3
4. Rg7+ Kf4 5. Rf7+ {[%also Rh7,Rc7,Rb7,Ra7,Rg6,Kg1,Kf2,Ke1,Re7]} 5... Kg3 6.
Ke1 {[%also Rg7+]} 6... f2+ 7. Rxf2 {Rxf2 — The pawn falls: a draw.} *

[Event "04. The Philidor: check from behind (3/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/3k1r2/2Rp4/8/3K4 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. The Philidor: check from behind (3/4)"]
[LineDescription "Once the pawn reaches your 3rd rank, check from far behind: the black king cannot hide."]

{[%csl Gc8,Gc7,Gc6] If Black blocks a check with its rook, a trade may be your
answer: your king is close enough to stop the pawn.} 1. Rc8 {[%also Rc7,Rc6]
Rc8! — Go far behind the king: check from a distance. Rc6 and Rc7 also hold.}
1... Ke3 2. Re8+ Re4 3. Rxe4+ {[%also Ra8,Rb8,Rc8,Rd8,Rf8,Rg8,Rh8]} 3... Kxe4 4.
Kd2 {Kd2! — Not Ke1: you end up in zugzwang.} 4... Kd4 5. Kd1 Kc3 6. Kc1 {Kc1! —
Black is in zugzwang: it must move, so it cannot win.} 6... d2+ 7. Kd1 Kb2 8.
Kxd2 {Kxd2 — The pawn falls: a draw.} *

[Event "04. The Philidor: check from behind (4/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/2r3k1/5p1R/8/4K3 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "04. The Philidor: check from behind (4/4)"]
[LineDescription "Once the pawn reaches your 3rd rank, check from far behind: the black king cannot hide."]

{[%csl Gh8,Gh7,Gh6] The last one before the exam.} 1. Rh8 {[%also Rh7,Rh6] Rh8!
— Go far behind the king: check from a distance. Rh6 and Rh7 also hold.} 1...
Kg3 2. Rg8+ Rg4 3. Rxg4+ Kxg4 4. Kf1 {[%also Kf2]} 4... Kh3 5. Kf2 {Kf2! — Not
Kg1: you end up in zugzwang.} 5... Kg4 6. Kf1 Kh4 7. Kf2 Kh3 8. Kxf3 {[%also
Kf1] Kxf3 — The pawn falls: a draw.} *

